    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s name comes from Mount Gilead in ancient Palestine, echoing a biblical reference common in 19th‑century America.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/gilead_nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "German pioneer Christian Luth first farmed near government roads around 1860, braving the harsh Great American Desert before Gilead’s formal founding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
